# Database Patterns & Entity Framework Core

## 🗄️ **Database Configuration**

### **Connection String Management:**
- **Key**: `ConnectionStrings__MSSQL` (double underscore for environment variables)
- **Provider**: Microsoft SQL Server (not PostgreSQL)
- **Format**: `Server=server,port;Database=dbname;User Id=user;Password=pass;TrustServerCertificate=true;MultipleActiveResultSets=true`

### **DbContext Configuration:**
```csharp
// Use ApplicationDbContext as the main context
public class ApplicationDbContext : IdentityDbContext<Account, IdentityRole<int>, int, ...>

// UTC DateTime conversion (configured globally)
protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder builder)
{
    UseUtc(builder); // Converts all DateTime to UTC
}
```

## 🏗️ **Entity Patterns**

### **Domain Entity Structure:**
```csharp
public class Account : IdentityUser<int>
{
    [MaxLength(50)]
    public string? RefreshToken { get; set; }
    
    public DateTime Created { get; set; }
    public DateTime LastUpdated { get; set; }
    
    // Navigation properties
    public ICollection<AccountTokenEntity> Tokens { get; set; }
    
    // Domain methods
    public bool IsLocked() => LockoutEnabled && LockoutEnd?.UtcDateTime > DateTime.UtcNow;
}
```

### **Entity Relationships:**
```csharp
// One-to-Many relationship
builder.Entity<AccountTokenEntity>()
    .HasOne(x => x.User)
    .WithMany(x => x.Tokens)
    .HasForeignKey(x => x.UserId);
```

## 🔄 **Migration Patterns**

### **Migration Commands:**
```bash
# Add new migration
dotnet ef migrations add MigrationName --project ApiTemplate.Infrastructure --startup-project ApiTemplate.Presentation.Web

# Update database
dotnet ef database update --project ApiTemplate.Infrastructure --startup-project ApiTemplate.Presentation.Web

# Remove last migration
dotnet ef migrations remove --project ApiTemplate.Infrastructure --startup-project ApiTemplate.Presentation.Web
```

### **Migration Best Practices:**
- Always review generated migration files before applying
- Use descriptive migration names
- Test migrations on development database first
- Keep migrations in `ApiTemplate.Infrastructure/Migrations/`

## 🔍 **Query Patterns**

### **Repository Implementation:**
```csharp
public class TRepository<T> : IRepository<T> where T : class
{
    protected readonly ApplicationDbContext _context;
    protected readonly DbSet<T> _dbSet;
    
    public async Task<T?> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _dbSet.FindAsync(id);
    }
    
    public async Task<IEnumerable<T>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _dbSet.ToListAsync();
    }
}
```

### **Query Optimization:**
```csharp
// Use AsNoTracking for read-only queries
var accounts = await _context.Accounts
    .AsNoTracking()
    .Where(a => a.IsActive)
    .ToListAsync();

// Use AsSplitQuery for multiple includes
var account = await _context.Accounts
    .Include(a => a.Tokens)
    .AsSplitQuery()
    .FirstOrDefaultAsync(a => a.Id == id);
```

